# manual checks of Authorization with a client token (Auth.http: register-client or client-login) or the panel
# cookie; the sender is the client of the token or the user of the cookie, each with only its own roles; a new account
# holds Identity.Owner on itself (scope Identity.User), a new client Identity.ClientOwner on itself (scope
# Identity.Client, its user too), both Plugins.Viewer on every plugin (ScopeId 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000)
@host = https://localhost:7105
@accessToken = paste-an-access-token
@clientId = paste-the-client-id-of-the-token
@otherClientId = paste-the-client-id-of-another-account

### every role the modules declare, with every permission (also of subordinate roles) and the roles it manages
GET {{host}}/authorization/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### the assignments of the sender
GET {{host}}/authorization/me/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### the client lets another client hold it as well (403 without identity.client.manage_access on the client)
POST {{host}}/authorization/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectId": "{{otherClientId}}", "roleCode": "Identity.ClientOwner", "scopeId": "{{clientId}}" }

### and takes it back
POST {{host}}/authorization/assignments/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectId": "{{otherClientId}}", "roleCode": "Identity.ClientOwner", "scopeId": "{{clientId}}" }
